# {{name}}

A [fudic](https://github.com/fudiePlatform/fudic) component library. It is **not** an
application: it has no routes, no `vite.config.ts` and no `sw.json`, because it is not
served — it is consumed.

## What it publishes

The `.fud` sources themselves, not a build. `exports` maps every component to its file, so
an app that depends on it links a component by package specifier:

```html
<link rel="component" href="{{name}}/card.fud">
```

That is why there is no `build` script here and why `files` carries `src`: a library ships
what the consumer's compiler reads.

## Adding a component

```sh
fudic g component card --project {{project}}
```

The `prefix` in `fudic.json` is what turns `card` into a tag. It proposes and does not
constrain — but a library is where it earns its keep, because its tags go on to live in the
global `customElements` registry of applications it does not control.
